Here is a draft of Claim 1 for the pulsed fluid nozzle arrangement:

***

1. A pulsed fluid nozzle arrangement comprising:

* a nozzle body defining a fluid inlet and a fluid outlet;
* a plunger movably disposed within the nozzle body, the plunger being biased by a spring element toward a first position;
* an annular seal positioned between the plunger and an interior surface of the nozzle body, the plunger and the annular seal together defining a mobile chamber wall;
* a fluid chamber bounding, at least in part, by the mobile chamber wall and arranged in fluid communication with the fluid inlet; and
* a prodder disposed within the fluid chamber and operatively coupled to the plunger for movement therewith relative to the fluid outlet;

wherein fluid pressure building within the fluid chamber acts against the mobile chamber wall to displace the plunger against a biasing force of the spring element, thereby moving the prodder relative to the fluid outlet to produce a pulsed fluid flow through the fluid outlet.
